# Host-level security headers.
# Netlify/Cloudflare Files apply `_headers` automatically; other hosts (Vercel,
# plain static) should replicate these in their own header config.
#
# Content-Security-Policy is intentionally NOT set here. The postbuild step
# (scripts/generate-security-headers.mjs) embeds a per-page CSP as a
# <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"> tag in every HTML document,
# hash-allowlisted to that page's own inline scripts. Keeping it in the
# document (rather than a ~60KB union header) makes it small and host-agnostic.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY